From: Value Fabric Security Team <security@valuefabric.io>
Date: 2026-05-27
Subject: [PATCH-002] STATUS: ALREADY FIXED — L1 Ingestion SSRF Validation

This patch documents that SSRF validation for callback URLs in Layer 1
Ingestion is ALREADY IMPLEMENTED in the current codebase.  No code
changes are required.

Current implementation (verified in main branch):

  File: services/layer1-ingestion/src/layer1_ingestion/api/main.py

  - ``_validate_callback_url_no_ssrf()`` function (lines ~360-400):
    * Blocks private IP ranges (10.x, 172.16-31.x, 192.168.x, 127.x,
      169.254.x)
    * Blocks cloud metadata endpoints (169.254.169.254,
      metadata.google.internal, metadata.internal)
    * Only allows ``https://`` scheme (http:// rejected)
    * Rejects localhost/loopback hostnames
    * Rejects URLs with non-HTTPS schemes (file://, ftp://, gopher://)
    * Uses ipaddress module to validate IP literals
    * Fails closed: any validation error raises ValueError

  - ``ExecuteTargetRequest`` Pydantic model (lines ~410-420):
    * Has ``@field_validator("callback_url")`` that calls
      ``_validate_callback_url_no_ssrf(v)``
    * Validates at API request time before any outbound call

  - ``_SSRF_BLOCKED_HOSTNAMES`` frozenset:
    * Static set of known-dangerous hostnames
    * Easy to extend for new cloud provider metadata endpoints

Security verification checklist:
  [x] Private IP ranges blocked
  [x] Metadata endpoints blocked
  [x] Only http:// and https:// allowed
  [x] file://, ftp://, gopher:// rejected
  [x] localhost/loopback rejected
  [x] URLs with username/password rejected (urlparse validation)
  [x] Fails closed (raises ValueError on any anomaly)

Status: NO PATCH REQUIRED — already production-ready.
Audit Ticket: SEC-2026-002 (closed)
